  },
  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "S2 keeps the 5% benchmark but gives already-marketed models an 18-month corrective-action and sales window with no numeric interim cap, which is the main concession to Northwind's 6.2% flagship. S3's 24-month start for new-unit shut-off and 6-year retrofit window favour Northwind, whose shut-off coverage is 38%. S5's 8-per-100k mandatory recall with no transition is the strongest consumer protection and bears most heavily on Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9."
 },
